# The Coliseum herald (demonstration dialogue, provisional).
dialogue.heraut-colisee.speaker = The Coliseum Herald
dialogue.heraut-colisee.presentation = Halt, traveller. You stand at the gates of the Arena of the Future. Here, two sides settle what a war would otherwise settle — and nobody leaves feet first. What are you looking for?
dialogue.heraut-colisee.presentation.marque = Nobody dies? How is that possible?
dialogue.heraut-colisee.presentation.inscription = I want to fight in the arena.
dialogue.heraut-colisee.presentation.partir = Nothing. I was only passing through.
dialogue.heraut-colisee.retour = You again. Still curious about the Mark, or do you finally want to fight?
dialogue.heraut-colisee.retour.marque = Tell me about the Mark again.
dialogue.heraut-colisee.retour.inscription = Put my name among the champions.
dialogue.heraut-colisee.retour.partir = I will be back.
dialogue.heraut-colisee.marque = Before every bout, a priest traces the Heroic Mark on each fighter. When the last blow falls, it raises everyone back up — winners and losers alike. Only Feargus fights without it.
dialogue.heraut-colisee.deja-inscrit = Your name is already on the list. Come back when the stands are full.
dialogue.heraut-colisee.demande = The champions' list is closed for the season. Unless you give me a good reason to reopen it.
dialogue.heraut-colisee.demande.convaincre = The stands crave fresh blood. I am what they are waiting for.
dialogue.heraut-colisee.demande.renoncer = Too bad. Another season.
dialogue.heraut-colisee.accepte-replique = Hm. You have nerve, and that is what the crowd loves. Your name is on the list — may the Mark keep you.
dialogue.heraut-colisee.refuse-replique = Fine speech. The list stays closed, and so does my patience.
dialogue.portier-colisee.speaker = The Coliseum gatekeeper
dialogue.portier-colisee.accueil = Nobody uses the great gate on a day without a bout. Still, you are here — come in. What do you want to know?
dialogue.portier-colisee.accueil.metier = Have you kept this gate long?
dialogue.portier-colisee.accueil.arene = What is really judged here?
dialogue.portier-colisee.accueil.partir = Nothing. I will walk a while.
dialogue.portier-colisee.metier = Thirty years. I have seen nobles walk in and leave in debt, and mercenaries walk in and leave as counts. The gate has not moved.
dialogue.portier-colisee.arene = Whatever the courts cannot settle. Two houses quarrelling over a vineyard, a charge without proof: the sand decides, and the Mark gives the bodies back.
dialogue.parieuse-tribunes.speaker = The stands bookmaker
dialogue.parieuse-tribunes.accueil = Three to one on the small one with the axe. Betting, or watching?
dialogue.parieuse-tribunes.accueil.metier = Do you live on these bets?
dialogue.parieuse-tribunes.accueil.arene = Who fights today?
dialogue.parieuse-tribunes.accueil.partir = Watching, thank you.
dialogue.parieuse-tribunes.metier = I live on them, and I have lived better. Since the Mark raises everyone, nobody bets on who dies — we bet on who yields. Subtler, and it pays less.
dialogue.parieuse-tribunes.arene = Nobody yet. The herald is waiting for a champion: go and talk to him if you have the shoulders, and I will change my odds.
dialogue.medecin-vestiaire.speaker = The locker-room physician
dialogue.medecin-vestiaire.accueil = Sit down if you are bleeding, stay standing if you are not. I have two hands and six fighters.
dialogue.medecin-vestiaire.accueil.metier = Is the Mark not enough, then?
dialogue.medecin-vestiaire.accueil.arene = Do you treat both sides?
dialogue.medecin-vestiaire.accueil.partir = I am not bleeding. Good day.
dialogue.medecin-vestiaire.metier = The Mark raises, it does not stitch. It gives the breath back and leaves the shoulder out, the rib cracked, the tooth broken. That part is my work.
dialogue.medecin-vestiaire.arene = Both, yes. A judgement is not a war: the loser goes home, and I would rather he walked there.
dialogue.vieux-gladiateur.speaker = The old gladiator
dialogue.vieux-gladiateur.accueil = You walk like someone who has never been down on the sand. It shows from here.
dialogue.vieux-gladiateur.accueil.metier = Have you been down there?
dialogue.vieux-gladiateur.accueil.arene = Any advice, then?
dialogue.vieux-gladiateur.accueil.partir = I will remember that.
dialogue.vieux-gladiateur.metier = Forty-one times. I won twenty-nine, and the other twelve taught me more. The Mark raised me twelve times; the knee never came back.
dialogue.vieux-gladiateur.arene = Two. Do not run for the middle: that is where the crowd wants you, and that is where two of them will take you. And watch the gates — they open.

